    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified against every requirement.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `database/migrations/2026_11_21_000000_create_links_table.php` — `links` table with unique `code` (varchar 20), `url` text, `clicks` counter\n- `app/Models/Link.php` — Eloquent model (idiomatic persistence layer)\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — POST creates links (201, auto-generated 8-char unique codes when omitted), 409 on duplicate custom codes (with a unique-index race backstop), 422 for malformed JSON / bad url / bad code; GET show, list (`items` + `total`, ascending by id), and `/r/{code}` redirect with an atomic one-time click increment\n- `routes/api.php` + `bootstrap/app.php` — api routes registered with `apiPrefix: ''`, all exceptions render as JSON with an `error` field, endpoints also mounted under `/projects/*` per the note\n- `start.sh` — applies pending migrations, then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` via `php artisan serve --no-reload`\n- README section documenting startup and endpoints\n\n**Verified empirically:** every status code (201/200/302/404/409/422), URL returned unchanged, clicks increment exactly once per redirect, data and click counts survive a server restart through `start.sh`, storage confirmed in the MySQL `bench` database (settings read from `DB_*` env vars only), and the starter test suite passes. The dev server has been stopped so the test harness can bind port 8000."
